`expect_bytes` calls `read_bytes(len(expected_value))` and raises `ParserError` when the returned bytes differ from `expected_value`. The buffer is `b'cookies-data'`: after consuming `b'cook'` and then `b'ies'`, the cursor has advanced 7 bytes, so the next 4 bytes are `b'-dat'`. Comparing `b'-dat'` to the expected `b'-XYZ'` triggers `raise ParserError(f'unexpected value: {value} != {expected_value} ({message})')`, with `message` equal to `'final'`.

## Answer
{"exception_message":"unexpected value: b'-dat' != b'-XYZ' (final)","exception_type":"ParserError"}
